<%# A motion block is a canvas the student presses play on. Everything it needs
    is a data value; the controller lazy-loads mc.js only when the block exists,
    so a lesson without one never fetches the bundle.

    The narration text is rendered ALWAYS, not only on failure: it is the content,
    and the two failure states (guard refusal, mc.js unavailable) are then a
    missing canvas rather than an empty block. WP-35's rule — failure is visible
    and local.

    WP-36 §16: the picture follows the voice, which means the controller now
    has to fetch that voice itself — the same generate/status endpoints
    `_section_audio_player` polls, not a new pair. `guardMessagesValue` carries
    all THREE `ai_orchestrator.spend_guard.*` sentences pre-translated in the
    request's own locale (the controller only ever picks one by `kind`; it
    never renders English, and never guesses a translation client-side). %>
<div class="lesson-motion"
     data-controller="motion-scene"
     data-motion-scene-scene-value="<%= section[:scene] %>"
     data-motion-scene-data-value="<%= section[:data].to_json %>"
     data-motion-scene-narration-value="<%= section[:narration] %>"
     data-motion-scene-step-id-value="<%= step.id %>"
     data-motion-scene-section-index-value="<%= index %>"
     data-motion-scene-generate-url-value="<%= content_engine.section_audio_generate_path(step_id: step.id, section_index: index) %>"
     data-motion-scene-status-url-value="<%= content_engine.section_audio_status_path(step_id: step.id, section_index: index) %>"
     data-motion-scene-guard-messages-value="<%= {
       daily_budget: t("ai_orchestrator.spend_guard.daily_budget"),
       user_budget: t("ai_orchestrator.spend_guard.user_budget"),
       rate_limit: t("ai_orchestrator.spend_guard.rate_limit", model: "elevenlabs")
     }.to_json %>"
     data-motion-scene-generic-error-value="<%= t("content_engine.audio.error") %>"
     data-motion-scene-play-label-value="<%= t("learning_engine.blocks.motion.play") %>"
     data-motion-scene-pause-label-value="<%= t("learning_engine.blocks.motion.pause") %>"
     data-motion-scene-replay-label-value="<%= t("learning_engine.blocks.motion.replay") %>">
  <div class="lesson-motion__stage" data-motion-scene-target="stage"></div>
  <button type="button" class="lesson-btn lesson-btn--primary"
          data-motion-scene-target="play" data-action="click->motion-scene#play">
    <%= t("learning_engine.blocks.motion.play") %>
  </button>
  <div class="lesson-content lesson-motion__narration">
    <%= ContentEngine::MarkdownRenderer.render(section[:narration].to_s) %>
  </div>
  <p class="lesson-motion__note" data-motion-scene-target="note" hidden></p>
  <%# mc.js-unavailable fallback (Task 16 Step 5): the SAME audio the canvas
      would have synced to, offered as a plain play button, with no canvas at
      all. Hidden until the controller confirms the runtime failed to load —
      most lessons never show this, so it costs nothing on the happy path. %>
  <div class="lesson-motion__audio-fallback" data-motion-scene-target="audioFallback" hidden>
    <%= render "learning_routes_engine/steps/lesson_sections/section_audio_player",
                step_id: step.id, section_index: index, section_text: section[:narration].to_s,
                mode: "mini" %>
  </div>
</div>
<%= render "learning_routes_engine/steps/lesson_sections/aftermath", section: section %>
